00:36:17,040 --> 00:36:22,670
思考和感觉就像是一个硬币的两面。
that thinking and feeling are two sides of the same coin.

676
00:36:22,670 --> 00:36:27,610
就像我们,外星人也许需要 感情。
Like us,aliens may<i> need</i> emotions.

677
00:36:30,920 --> 00:36:34,520
科幻中经常描绘发达的外星种族
Science fiction often depicts advanced alien species

678
00:36:34,520 --> 00:36:38,460
是一些冰冷无情的纯粹智慧的生物--
as cold,emotionless beings of pure intellect --

679
00:36:38,460 --> 00:36:41,400
基本上就像是长着腿的电脑。
basically,computers with legs.

680
00:36:41,400 --> 00:36:44,500
根据这样推理,
According to this line of reasoning,

681
00:36:44,500 --> 00:36:49,270
情感是可以混乱我们思维的原始冲动。
emotions are primitive urges that merely cloud our thinking.

682
00:36:49,270 --> 00:36:51,940
但是一个精神力发达的种族
But would a mentally superior species

683
00:36:51,940 --> 00:36:54,840
就不需要有感情吗？
necessarily be devoid of feelings?

684
00:36:54,840 --> 00:36:58,050
还是他们也有情感？
Or could aliens have a heart?

685
00:37:05,050 --> 00:37:09,220
心理学家Lisa Barrett开拓性的研究
Psychologist Lisa Barrett's groundbreaking research

686
00:37:09,220 --> 00:37:13,760
表明语言、记忆、甚至理性思维
reveals that language,memory,and even rational thought

687
00:37:13,760 --> 00:37:15,960
全部依赖于情感。
all depend upon emotion.

688
00:37:15,960 --> 00:37:18,230
Barrett：当你感到气愤时,
Barrett: When you feel angry,

689
00:37:18,230 --> 00:37:19,400
你会有这种
you experience this

690
00:37:19,400 --> 00:37:22,070
和你有着像美丽花朵的记忆、
as very different from when you're having a memory

691
00:37:22,070 --> 00:37:24,710
或当你想着一些或察觉一些
or when you're thinking something

692
00:37:24,710 --> 00:37:27,440
像美丽花朵一样的东西时
or when you're perceiving something

693
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:28,680
完全不同的体会。
like a beautiful flower.

694
00:37:28,680 --> 00:37:29,880
这些你觉得
Those seem to you

695
00:37:29,880 --> 00:37:32,040
非常非常不同的感受,
to be very,very different kinds of experiences,

696
00:37:32,050 --> 00:37:36,720
在大脑水平实际上是通过相同的网络进行的,
but at the level of the brain,there are common networks

697
00:37:36,720 --> 00:37:40,450
这些网络在所有这类刺激下都会激活。
that are active during all of those events.

698
00:37:40,450 --> 00:37:44,020
弗里曼：这种情感和理性思维
Freeman: The notion that our emotional and rational minds

699
00:37:44,020 --> 00:37:46,530
是完全分开的理念
are entirely separate

700
00:37:46,530 --> 00:37:48,030
可以追溯到柏拉图,
dates black to Plato,

701
00:37:48,030 --> 00:37:51,200
他认为情感是野蛮残暴的本能。
who saw emotions as savage,brutish instincts.

702
00:37:51,200 --> 00:37:53,230
[呻吟声]
[ Groans ]

703
00:37:53,230 --> 00:37:54,800
查尔斯·达尔文也认为
Charles Darwin argued

704
00:37:54,800 --> 00:37:58,410
情感是人类从动物开始尚未进化掉的残余,
that emotions are evolutionary holdovers from animals

705
00:37:58,410 --> 00:38:00,610
对于目的不再有用,
which no longer serve any useful purpose,

706
00:38:00,610 --> 00:38:03,310
就像我们残留的尾椎骨,
like our vestigial tailbones.

707
00:38:03,310 --> 00:38:05,380
人类的未来,
Humans of the future,

708
00:38:05,380 --> 00:38:09,650
或是已经进化许久的外星种族
or any alien species far along the evolutionary trail,

709
00:38:09,650 --> 00:38:11,620
不会再有情感的压力。
will not be burdened with feelings.

710
00:38:11,620 --> 00:38:13,920
但根据Lisa的观点,
But according to Lisa,

711
00:38:13,920 --> 00:38:17,990
你无法将理性与感性区分开。
you can't separate reason from emotion.

712
00:38:22,060 --> 00:38:25,170
她在东北大学的实验室中,
In her lab at northeastern university,

713
00:38:25,170 --> 00:38:28,400
Lisa研究了情感如何塑造思维。
Lisa studies how emotions shape thought.

714
00:38:28,400 --> 00:38:31,970
她通过改变人们的核心情绪--
She does this by altering people's core affect --

715
00:38:31,970 --> 00:38:35,940
在复杂感情下思维的基本状态,
the basic state of mind that underlies complex emotions,

716
00:38:35,940 --> 00:38:40,580
而她在他们察觉不到的情况下进行。
and she does this without their knowing it.

717
00:38:40,580 --> 00:38:43,480
Barrett: 受试者来到实验室中,
Barrett: So,subjects come into the laboratory,

718
00:38:43,480 --> 00:38:45,390
通过一些专业设备仪器,
and using specialized equipment,

719
00:38:45,390 --> 00:38:48,860
我们给他们左右眼分别展示不同的图像,
we present different images to the left and the right eye.

720
00:38:48,860 --> 00:38:52,160
一个眼中,我们会呈现闪烁的图像--
To one eye,we will present flashing images --

721
00:38:52,160 --> 00:38:55,700
我们可以说是蒙德里安风格的艺术图像--
let's say mondrian-type image of artwork --

722
00:38:55,700 --> 00:38:58,430
其中隐藏着视觉噪音。
embedded in visual noise.

723
00:38:58,430 --> 00:39:01,200
我们会给另一只眼一幅静态图,
To the other eye,we present a static image

724
00:39:01,200 --> 00:39:04,140
无表情的脸、微笑的脸、
of either a neutral face,a smiling face,

725
00:39:04,140 --> 00:39:06,240
或是发愁的脸。
or a scowling face.

726
00:39:06,240 --> 00:39:09,480
弗里曼：当你的一只眼看闪动的图片
Freeman: When one of your eyes is shown a flashing image

727
00:39:09,480 --> 00:39:11,980
另一只眼看静态图时,
and the other eye is shown a still image,

728
00:39:11,980 --> 00:39:15,820
你就会有意识的去看闪动图,
you are only conscious of seeing the flashing image,

729
00:39:15,820 --> 00:39:20,350
而静态图会进入你的潜意识思维中。
but the still image nonetheless reaches your subconscious mind.

730
00:39:24,960 --> 00:39:29,800
通过测量皮肤传导、心跳速率、呼吸和
By measuring skin conduction,heart rate,breathing,

731
00:39:29,800 --> 00:39:31,630
血管阻力,
and vascular resistance,

732
00:39:31,630 --> 00:39:35,000
Lisa检测了她的受试者对隐藏表情
Lisa detects her subjects' unconscious responses

733
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,840
的无意识反应,
to the hidden faces

734
00:39:36,840 --> 00:39:41,040
然后测量了这会如何影响他们的思考。
and then measures how this affects their thinking.

735
00:39:41,040 --> 00:39:45,910
她发现看着微笑的静态图的人们
She's found that people exposed to the static smiling face

736
00:39:45,910 --> 00:39:50,320
更可能会发现蒙德里安式图片的美,
are more likely to find the mondrian-type image beautiful.

737
00:39:50,320 --> 00:39:53,890
当隐藏的表情是皱眉时,
But when the hidden face is frowning,

738
00:39:53,890 --> 00:39:56,060
他们则不喜欢这张图片。
they don't like the picture.

739
00:39:56,060 --> 00:39:57,360
在这个世界中
It's not the case

740
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:59,690
我们并不是无感情的看待事物
that we're impassively viewing things in the world

741
00:39:59,690 --> 00:40:02,060
然后才对它们有反应。
and then having reactions to them.

742
00:40:02,060 --> 00:40:04,000
我们看到的,
Our affective feelings

743
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:06,770
以及如何判断看到的,
are actually influencing what we see

744
00:40:06,770 --> 00:40:09,470
实际上都会影响我们的情绪感受。
and how we make judgments about what we see.

745
00:40:11,940 --> 00:40:13,840
弗里曼：无论我们是否知道,
Freeman: Whether we know it or not,

746
00:40:13,840 --> 00:40:19,310
情感决定了我们如何思考,以及我们会注意什么。
emotions determine how we think and what we pay attention to.

747
00:40:19,310 --> 00:40:23,280
你的情绪帮助你分配注意力,
Your affect helps you to allocate your attention,

748
00:40:23,280 --> 00:40:25,250
比如说,对于我来说
for example,towards me

749
00:40:25,250 --> 00:40:28,460
忽视其他所有的信息来源,
and ignore all the other sources of information

750
00:40:28,460 --> 00:40:31,290
你就能够集中注意力听我说。
that you could potentially be paying attention to.

751
00:40:31,290 --> 00:40:34,630
情绪同样使你增强感知
Affect also helps you to sharpen your perception

752
00:40:34,630 --> 00:40:37,860
专注于你要注意的东西。
of the thing you're paying attention to.

753
00:40:37,860 --> 00:40:40,200
弗里曼：如果情感是
Freeman: If emotions are essential

754
00:40:40,200 --> 00:40:42,640
意识和自我意识的要素,
to consciousness and self-awareness,

755
00:40:42,640 --> 00:40:45,740
那么外星人就当然会拥有感情。
then aliens will certainly have them.

756
00:40:45,740 --> 00:40:50,480
他们会像我们一样使用感情--
They will use them the same way we do --

757
00:40:50,480 --> 00:40:52,950
来实现自己的目标...
to realize their goals...

758
00:40:52,950 --> 00:40:54,610
液(字幕君丧失中...)！
Yay!

759
00:40:54,610 --> 00:40:58,050
来定义他们的人格个性...
...to define their personalities...

760
00:40:58,050 --> 00:41:00,120
[咕哝声]
[ Grunts ]

761
00:41:00,120 --> 00:41:02,160
...来使他们的世界合理。
...to make sense of their world.

762
00:41:03,790 --> 00:41:06,230
真正的外星人思维
The true nature of alien thought

763
00:41:06,230 --> 00:41:09,600
也许会推翻我们的猜测,
would probably defy our speculations.

764
00:41:09,600 --> 00:41:12,600
它可能会超越我们的理解范畴,
It may well be beyond our understanding,

765
00:41:12,600 --> 00:41:16,470
但通过对地球上另类思维的研究,
but by studying the minds of the aliens here on earth,

766
00:41:16,470 --> 00:41:18,640
我们对自己、
we have learned much about ourselves

767
00:41:18,640 --> 00:41:21,170
对大自然赋予我们的
and the gift of having brains

768
00:41:21,170 --> 00:41:25,680
可以思考感觉和交流的脑了解更多。
that can think,feel,and communicate.

769
00:41:28,550 --> 00:41:33,420
某一天,当我们最终和外星思维接触时,
One day,when we finally engage with alien minds,

770
00:41:33,420 --> 00:41:34,690
我们也许会明白
we will find out

771
00:41:34,690 --> 00:41:38,120
到底意识、感情和想象是我们特有的,
whether consciousness,emotion,and imagination

772
00:41:38,120 --> 00:41:42,630
还是众星中普遍存在的。
are unique to us or spread throughout the stars.

773
00:41:42,630 --> 00:41:45,800
可是现在,我们还没有办法知道,
Right now,we have no way of knowing.

774
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:50,740
我们唯独能做的就是想象。
All we can do is imagine.

